TD=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;sys.path.insert(0,str(TD.parent))
from manuscript_support import build
E=[
('01-00','State and government','A state is an enduring political organisation with territory, population and governing institutions; a government exercises public power through those institutions.','Rules, representation and accountability influence whose needs affect public decisions. A change of government does not necessarily create a different state.'),
('01-01','Constitution','A constitution is the fundamental rules establishing how a state is organised, how public power is exercised and the rights recognised.','It differs from an ordinary policy and requires implementation and accountability to influence lived access.'),
('01-02','Authority','Authority is recognised legitimacy to make decisions or exercise power within a specified role.','An authorised officer can have limited resources; formal authority differs from the practical capacity to influence outcomes.'),
('01-03','Power','Power is the capacity to influence actions or outcomes; it can exist without recognised legitimate authority.','A person may exert influence through resources or pressure without holding the authorised role.'),
('01-04','Representation','Representation is acting or speaking on behalf of others in decision-making.','Meaningful representation needs communication and accountability to those represented, rather than presence alone.'),
('01-05','Delegation','Delegation assigns a task or decision responsibility to another person or body within defined limits.','Clear limits, resources and reporting matter; assigning work without means to perform it may fail.'),
('01-06','Election','An election is a process for choosing representatives or office holders through voting.','Fair choice also depends on accessible participation, information and credible procedures.'),
('01-07','Voting','Voting is expressing a choice in an election or collective decision under its rules.','A vote records a choice, while representation concerns subsequent decisions on others’ behalf.'),
('02-00','Types can overlap','Government types describe different features such as head of state, accountability and concentration of power.','A republic can be democratic or authoritarian; a constitutional monarchy may coexist with parliamentary democracy. Do not treat the labels as mutually exclusive.'),
('02-01','Monarchy','A monarchy has a monarch as head of state, commonly through hereditary succession.','The monarch’s powers vary; the title alone does not establish absolute control.'),
('02-02','Parliamentary democracy','Parliamentary democracy bases democratic government on an elected parliament to which the executive is accountable.','Voting, scrutiny and rights need effective practice; the name alone does not establish equal influence.'),
('02-03','Republic','A republic has a non-hereditary public office as head of state rather than a monarch.','This does not by itself establish free elections or limits on executive power.'),
('02-04','One-party state','A one-party state permits political rule through a single authorised party without genuine competitive party alternation.','Restricted competition limits voters’ alternatives; compare actual accountability and participation.'),
('02-05','Dictatorship','A dictatorship concentrates political power with weak or absent effective democratic checks and competition.','It differs from authority exercised within accountable limits; announced efficiency does not establish development benefit.'),
('02-06','Totalitarianism','Totalitarianism seeks pervasive control over political and wider social life, often through a dominant ideology and coercive institutions.','It describes an extent of control beyond the mere presence of a strong executive; avoid inferring it from one policy.'),
('03-00','Ownership and ideology','Capitalism, socialism, mixed economies and communism concern productive ownership and coordination in differing ways; fascism also concerns authoritarian political ideology.','Economic and political classifications are separate. Private enterprise can coexist with public services and regulation.'),
('03-01','Capitalism','Capitalism emphasises private ownership of productive resources and market allocation.','Regulation and public activity can still exist; the label does not imply no state role.'),
('03-02','Socialism','Socialism emphasises social ownership or control and collective provision or distribution aims, in varied forms.','It is not a single institutional arrangement or a synonym for any public service.'),
('03-03','Mixed economy','A mixed economy combines private and public economic activity and different roles for markets and public decisions.','The balance varies; a state-owned provider alongside private producers distinguishes it from an exclusively private arrangement.'),
('03-04','Communism','Communism as an economic ideal involves common ownership of productive resources and a classless society.','Historically labelled communist states have generally used extensive state ownership and planning; the ideal and actual institutions should be distinguished.'),
('03-05','Fascism','Fascism is an authoritarian ultranationalist ideology emphasising concentrated leadership, suppression of opposition and subordinating individuals to the state or nation.','It is not merely another word for government intervention or a mixed economy.'),
('04-00','Public conditions for development','Government and regional or local institutions can support peace, opportunities, infrastructure, education and social services.','For a Namibian application, connect the level’s resources and responsibilities to actual access; an announced allocation is not delivered provision.'),
('04-01','Peace and security','Safety can allow production, travel, learning and public participation to continue.','Security pursued without accountable protection can itself restrict rights; judge who can use the resulting opportunities.'),
('04-02','Opportunities and finance','Publicly supported credit or training can address missing productive resources.','Repayment, eligibility and viable demand matter; a loan cannot by itself repair a market or skills gap.'),
('04-03','Infrastructure','Infrastructure provides supporting networks such as water, roads, electricity and communications.','Maintenance and usable connections turn installed assets into services; a disconnected network segment may not remove the barrier.'),
('04-04','Education and social services','Education and social provision can build capabilities and protect well-being.','Staff, supplies, access and inclusion determine use; building counts alone cannot establish outcomes.'),
('04-05','Decentralisation','Decentralisation transfers specified functions or decision responsibilities from central to subnational levels.','Local knowledge can improve relevance if resources, capacity and accountability accompany functions; transfer without funding can leave a service gap.'),
('05-00','Implementation barriers','Planning, skills, ethics, finance and continued training affect how resources become development outcomes.','These are mechanisms to investigate, not proof that all people in a lower-income country lack effort or integrity.'),
('05-01','Planning','Poor planning can mismatch activities, resources and actual needs.','An unused facility may result when staffing or access was omitted; checking the need and operating resources can prevent a construction-only response.'),
('05-02','Skills','Missing relevant skills can prevent productive equipment or services operating effectively.','Recruitment and accessible training can address a documented gap, while more equipment alone may remain idle.'),
('05-03','Ethics and transparency','Corruption diverts entrusted decisions or resources for improper benefit; transparency makes decisions and resource use open to scrutiny.','Clear records and accountability can help detect diversion, but publishing a budget alone does not ensure effective oversight.'),
('05-04','Finance','Insufficient finance can stop feasible inputs or maintenance being obtained.','Identify the missing resource and sustainable funding route; borrowing without viable returns can add repayment pressure.'),
('05-05','In-service training','In-service training updates skills during employment.','Relevant practice and support can help staff use changed procedures; a one-off certificate without application need not improve performance.')]
